Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 10:28:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(redirect): restrict URL redirects to credential-free
 HTTP

Context:
- The /u/ role accepted every URL scheme recognized by the platform parser, including executable or local-resource schemes.
- Credential-bearing HTTP(S) URLs could also expose userinfo through redirects.

Expected behavior:
- /u/ redirects accept only absolute http: and https: URLs without username or password components.
- Valid HTTP(S) redirects preserve existing redirect behavior, including paths and queries.
- Malformed URLs, non-HTTP(S) schemes, and credential-bearing URLs return 400.

Acceptance criteria:
- [x] Valid HTTP and HTTPS URLs redirect.
- [x] Non-HTTP(S) schemes are rejected.
- [x] HTTP(S) credentials/userinfo are rejected.
- [x] Malformed URL and existing overlong URL rejection remain covered.

Constraints:
- Generic upstream patch only; no Feishu-specific behavior.
- No generalized URL-security redesign or unrelated redirect features.
- Keep the existing generic frontend URL check unchanged.

Validation:
- RED: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run worker/test/roles.spec.ts; 8 new security cases returned 302 instead of expected 400.
- GREEN: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run worker/test/roles.spec.ts; 15/15 passed.
- REFACTOR: Prettier and TypeScript checks passed after introducing the redirect-specific helper.
- REGRESSION: ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run --project Workers; 124/124 passed.
- REGRESSION: ESLint, Prettier check, TypeScript, Wrangler dry-run build, and git diff --check passed.
- Note: the full combined suite is locally blocked by Node 26 localStorage behavior in pre-existing frontend tests; Worker scope is fully green and CI will run the repository environment.

Docs:
- N/A; behavior and regression cases are self-contained in the narrow security patch. Promotion provenance will document the carried patch.

